{"name":"Sticks & Stones","hex":"#baa482","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sticks","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of stick"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["rural terrain, especially a woody area; any rural region.","Hurdles or other obstacles to be jumped over."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sticks"},{"term":"stones","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of stone"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Testicles; balls.","Courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stones"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sticks & Stones (2019 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Sticks & Stones is a 2019 American stand-up comedy television special starring comedian Dave Chappelle and directed by Stan Lathan. It was produced by Chappelle and Lathan and distributed by Netflix, the special is detailed as \"a provocative perspective on the tidal wave of celebrity scandals, the opioid crisis, and more\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/96/Dave_Chappelle%2C_Sticks_%26_Stones_%282019%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sticks_%26_Stones_(2019_film)"},{"title":"Sticks & Stones (Arlissa song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Sticks & Stones\" is a song by British singer and songwriter Arlissa, released on 3 March 2013 as the lead single from her scrapped debut album, Battles. The song was written by Arlissa, Mark Taylor, Patrick Mascall and Jamie Scott. It peaked at number 48 on the UK Singles Chart for the week ending 16 March 2013 and spent 3 weeks in the top 100."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/be/Arlissa_-_Sticks_and_Stones.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sticks_%26_Stones_(Arlissa_song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/96/Dave_Chappelle%2C_Sticks_%26_Stones_%28201